0..54 Comment "// What is not open stays at the world it was made at."
55..57 Comment "//"
58..133 Comment "// A handle crosses as the content of the value it holds. A thunk names its"
134..207 Comment "// environment by location, so its bytes mean nothing at another world. A"
208..283 Comment "// handle to one is not open, and a value holding one is not mobile either."
284..286 Comment "//"
287..363 Comment "// Each declaration migrates to the seat and returns what it made there. The"
364..441 Comment "// refusal names the judgement that fails: `NotOpen` for what a handle holds,"
442..482 Comment "// `Immobile` for a former met directly."
483..485 Comment "//"
486..562 Comment "// - see: Rainey et al., \"LoCalMem\", PACMPL 10 (ICFP 2026), § 5.1, openness"
563..623 Comment "// - see: `model/worlds/open.gandr` — what is open crosses"
625..691 Comment "// The operator\'s and the seat\'s worlds, each declaration\'s entry."
